 without quantified incidence percentages.","reason":"Remove unsupported '0%' wording while retaining FDA-label adverse reaction facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/009170Orig1s040lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not provide a half-life value.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"10-15 hours for primidone; may increase in patients older than 75 years.","reason":"Trusted NCBI source provides a half-life value.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562297/"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not identify a major metabolic organ; label identifies phenobarbital and PEMA metabolites.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver; primidone is extensively metabolized by the liver to phenobarbital and PEMA, with substantial unchanged urinary excretion.","reason":"Trusted NCBI sources contradict the limited/unknown metabolism wording.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548512/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562297/"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA label does not define clinically meaningful enzyme induction or inhibition.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Enzyme inducer: NCBI LiverTox states primidone can induce CYP450 enzyme activities; StatPearls notes hepatic metabolism and phenobarbital-related induction of UGT/CYP2C/CYP3A pathways.","reason":"Trusted NCBI sources support enzyme induction.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548512/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562297/"]},{"current_value":"Unknown/limited","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Enzyme inducer","reason":"Align filter with NCBI-supported induction evidence.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK54